    "text": "The Goborchinn are an Irish mythological race. They form a branch of the Fomorians. Eochaid Echchenn, whose name means horse-head, ruled them. The Fomorians always connect to the sea. So the Goborchinn may tie to the water horse. The Book of Invasions tells of the Goborchinn. Some read that text as a record of real immigration to Ireland. They suggest the Fomorians were a pre-Celtic people. The Goborchinn formed part of that people.",
